{"title":"2005 IMO Problems/Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/a/75a2d6d47afcf79e8493b06e33a20204d7102354.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1, a_2, \\dots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"70\" height=\"11\" /> be a sequence of integers with infinitely many positive and negative terms. Suppose that for every positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> the numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/1/f81465f6b02301397dd62f8fabd0eb65bc53077b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1, a_2, \\dots, a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"100\" height=\"11\" /> leave <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> different remainders upon division by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. Prove that every integer occurs exactly once in the sequence.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/7/947fd1bff2c2636689eef0f4c78fb70044da9eac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${a_n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"10\" /> satisfies the conditions if and only if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/c/55c81beaab0fae69a4d84710d525c5c949d9ea8b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${a_n-a_1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"15\" /> does.\nTherefore we can assume that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/b/84b16161509fc81d43ce3983057c5f36feba3fa7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>First of all, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/0/320f9c6c92171cb9d5f8055e151d5de0f2e31ef2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|a_n|&lt;n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"66\" height=\"20\" />\nOtherwise, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/8/00839c159e992246a3674bfeefb7c69183903622.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"15\" /> mod <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/6/dc6ada4bfbe785227f8d26b5a7088d62c66332fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{a_n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"28\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><br />\nClaim: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/b/51bb8f97be092c275f4636c0782c3b93b3c69df8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{k+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"12\" /> is either the smallest positive number not in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/7/cc71f755ab462abd9b792a57bebb0c701e049996.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${a_1, a_2, ..., a_k}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"93\" height=\"13\" /> or the largest negative number not in this set.\n</p>\n<ul><li>Proof by induction: the induction hypothesis implies that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/a/69ab7e271211468bf825a25e28f02b931fe1777f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1, a_2, ..., a_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"93\" height=\"13\" /> are consecutive. Let m and M be the smallest and largest numbers in this consecutive set, respectively. It is clear that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/2/e32f9926e18bf252801dbed4bb8510988404fa91.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{k+1}=m-1=M+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"183\" height=\"18\" /> mod <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/5/f05f085f774fc8ab50676b778b86a1f1d1114fc8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" />. But since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/0/320f9c6c92171cb9d5f8055e151d5de0f2e31ef2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|a_n|&lt;n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"66\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/e/86ec28c4040acb9d889dc86b92347349cdee99f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{k+1}=m-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"108\" height=\"18\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/e/afe144e5517842d0ce8986c6fada40267e99bd6d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"53\" height=\"16\" /></li></ul>\n<p><br />\nThis proves that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/7/947fd1bff2c2636689eef0f4c78fb70044da9eac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${a_n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"10\" /> contains an infinite number of positive and negative numbers, it must contain each integer exactly once.\n</p><p>~Kscv\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_IMO\" title=\"2005 IMO\">2005 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_IMO_Problems\" title=\"2005 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2005 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2005 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2005 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2005 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2005 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2005 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2005 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017092508\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.019 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.031 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 135/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 894/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 44/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0